#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:5
#: 9e9ac818b8614293ab4a0eccee8be01b
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:7
#: c8addf9384b54a65a57e093a7438d379
msgid "The antenna tracker requires much of the same basic configuration as Copter and Plane and then some specific configuration specific to the antenna tracker. Below are the details of this set-up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:14
#: 20614b93879a43d0b6087c197a8c9d28
msgid "Setting the AHRS orientation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:16
#: fffdd78563f140608d692043a1dd0a35
msgid "If the flight controller board could not be mounted so that its forward direction is aligned with the antenna (as mentioned on the :ref:`Assembling a frame page <frame-assembly>`) the AHRS_ORIENTATION parameter should be set from the Mission Planner's Config/Tuning >> Advanced Params screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:24
#: 17e0f9c731f746af858abc6faab72103
msgid "Some commonly used values include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:26
#: e6cdd7229c74487789dafa0e267839c1
msgid "Pitch90 : the flight controller is pointing up at 90 degrees compared to the direction of the antenna"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:28
#: 4658b32da0c64b37b9c4e8a7b7747c75
msgid "Pitch270 : the flight controller is pointing down at 90 degrees compared to the direction of the antenna"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:32
#: b5cd60ef83cc42098637dcdd37f03e02
msgid "Accelerometer Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:34
#: 4f95e2a3695a43d8875f01472e372829
msgid "The :ref:`accelerometer calibration <copter:common-accelerometer-calibration>` is the same as for Copter meaning the flight controller board should be connected to the Mission planner and then the **Initial Setup \\| Mandatory Hardware \\| Accel Calibration** routine should be run which involves holding the board in 6 separate orientations positions so that offsets and scaling can be calculated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:44
#: 0e0134a43bc748949014a4a85cec29d4
msgid "Setting the Compass orientation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:46
#: ff62e1c714384463aaec756c5e7e3238
msgid "If an external GPS+compass module is being used but the arrow on the case could not be aligned so as to point in the same direction as the antenna, the COMPASS_ORIENTATION parameter should be set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:53
#: 0220f21b44dc4eab8de4382d23d27364
msgid "Some more commonly used values include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:55
#: 3a0481910e464f7d80f6d7e91b86e7a5
msgid "Yaw 90 : the arrow on the compass module is pointing off to the right at a 90 degree angle clockwise from the direction the antenna is pointing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:58
#: 4a9907224df849e292ca06cf54caedfb
msgid "Yaw 270: the arrow is pointing to the left at 90degrees from the antenna. I.e. the arrow is rotated at 90deg counter-clockwise from where the antenna is pointed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:63
#: 7e2f2e945ea34ee88cb399796154a7c2
msgid "Compass Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:65
#: d6ebe7021e6e442ab88c2482da8c2bc4
msgid "The :ref:`compass calibration <copter:common-compass-calibration-in-mission-planner>` can be done using the same method as Copter.  Open the Mission Planner's Initial Setup >> Mandatory Hardware >> Compass screen and push the \"Live Calibration\" button and rotate the board until the mission planner says it has captured enough points to correctly calculate the offsets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:72
#: 4bc9dd4b9aee4541a2c4fb9e2077b65e
msgid "Setting the servo and range of movement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:74
#: 4f6f2369137441ff92818b745a7aa2d7
msgid "For this section it is best to plug in the battery so that the servos are powered and push the \"arming switch\" if present.  Connect with the Mission Planner, go to the CONFIG/TUNING >> Extended Tuning page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:82
#: cd63f0159ce645f0bff0a1335d2181c5
msgid "Setting the Yaw servo's min and max pwm values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:84
#: 25b895a0f1af415aba73e8cfc74f9cb9
msgid "The green \"Test\" buttons on this screen work in conjunction with the Min, Max field values and the slider position.  If the slider is pushed all the way to the left and the Test button is pushed, the pwm value in the \"Min\" field will be sent to the servo.  If the slider is pushed all the way to the right and the Test button is pushed, the pwm value in the Max field will be sent to the servo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:91
#: 94fd85e838a7445ea49b4743d1235ac8
msgid "If the Yaw (aka pan) servo's minimum and maximum pwm values are known, they can simply be entered into the Yaw Servo Min and Max fields.  If they are not know, you can discover them through experimentation.  For example to discover the minimum, push the slider all the way to the left and then enter progressively lower pwm values (pushing the Test button after each change) until you discover the lowest value that causes the servos to move. Repeat for the Max field by pushing the slider all the way to the right and entering progressively higher pwm values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:100
#: 4150781892e0427e85848cd4211c5fdf
msgid "Normally lower pwm values should cause the tracker to point to the right (i.e. clockwise), higher values will point to the left (i.e. counter-clockwise).  If this is not the case, the \"Reverse\" checkbox should be checked.  Note that changing this checkbox will not affect how the tracker operates when using the Test button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:106
#: d45e96597b34436d8ff01289ae4cf8fb
msgid "The Neutral field is the value that will be output to the servos when the tracker first begins controlling them after startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:110
#: 495602089e174400b772c509bc74ecd2
msgid "Setting the Yaw servo's range of movement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:112
#: 901693bbb0fd4334b3401cf669595b22
msgid "In this step we want to discover the heading change that comes from moving the servos between their minimum and maximum  values. One way to do this is to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:116
#: dc1bb01810d54a8ead24f7cd7ca4baaa
msgid "Put the slider all the way to the left (if the Reverse checkbox is unchecked) or right (if the Reverse checkbox is checked) and push the Test button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:119
#: 7a9793b5b36541258958a301806f42a2
msgid "Rotate the tracker so that its heading (on the MP's Flight Data screen) shows close to \"0\" (i.e. North)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:121
#: 4e984f3cf40b4c15a002bfd38a12f466
msgid "Return to the extended tuning page, push the slider all the way to the other extreme and push Test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:123
#: f3c96b3cafc14deb80ad8c73d2a25fc3
msgid "The new heading back on the Flight Data screen is the range of movement and should be entered into the \"Range of movement field\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:127
#: a39e5f32acf144b4b9e183b4f7b37872
msgid "Setting the Pitch servo's range of movement pwm values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:129
#: 0eff3cf293b54a7da92bd68e6400de35
msgid "Repeat the procedures described above to discover the Yaw servo's min and max values except using the fields and buttons in the \"Pitch Servo\" section of the Extended Tuning screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:133
#: a5c2e38b1e07443fb4086b0f7098dc8e
msgid "Lower pwm values should cause the tracker to aim down, higher pwm values to aim up.  If this is not the case, the \"Reverse\" checkbox should be checked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:138
#: 1f267e1f9ac4424787cdf8e2effc7a41
msgid "Setting the Pitch servo's range of movement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:140
#: 7afa55812de44fdd9e6314716ba1dedd
msgid "Repeat the procedures used to discover the Yaw servo's range of movement except that the difference in the Pitch values shown on the Mission Planner's Flight Data screen should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:145
#: 64778c7b71714c15b855af84cfcb2a33
msgid "Manually setting the parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:147
#: b33b712a9fd949978bfd207158f639b0
msgid "If the mission planner is not being used the parameters below can be updated manually:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:150
#: 5c500b70c3e74c048dee33543b98c84a
msgid "RC1\\_ parameters control the pan (aka yaw) servo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:152
#: 7134972b3620453dbd69018d69f57f1d
msgid "RC1_MIN : min pwm value that can be sent to the pan servo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:154
#: cf82e721d1614a2d816a063086ac8083
msgid "RC1_MAX : max pwm value that can be sent to the pan servo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:156
#: b6e160f1717b4e41afc6c52737076a7c
msgid "RC1_REV : set to \"-1\" if the tracker rotates in the wrong direction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:158
#: 69c99f95f2a24c058441cd45871b3105
msgid "RC2\\_ parameters control the tilt (aka pitch) servo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:160
#: 22d96be8925c41e3bb4bb3203f888e07
msgid "RC2_MIN : min pwm value that can be sent to the tilt servo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:162
#: c569905f30a84422b14dbfecf5e3dc80
msgid "RC2_MAX : max pwm value that can be sent to the tilt servo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:164
#: 7329d639e9b242b88a535bfb223e3b03
msgid "RC2_REV : set to \"-1\" if the tracker tilts in the wrong direction (i.e. tilts down when vehicle is above tracker)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:169
#: 1b8e2c6a2def478faa650d5c8d074cf6
msgid "For continuous rotation set YAW_RANGE equal to 360.  Make sure you hardware setup (i.e. the cabling) can handle the tracker turning continuous circles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:174
#: 884796e5e9494e5ea99da354de776808
msgid "Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:176
#: e30d239bf303445c90fd6a4d44134fa4
msgid "YAW2SRV_P, I and D values are set the pan control's gains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/configuration.rst:178
#: 5d2b2464af7644f7b1d4bf41e17e7ace
msgid "PITCH2SRV_P, I and D values are set the tilt control's gains."
msgstr ""
